{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109080","id":2704282489,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6hMBN5","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109080.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109080/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109080/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109080/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d8eea1ea1c5e87d33762766775c867832e4fc500","number":109080,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[DRAFT] Support multi-threaded rendering with OpenGL on Android","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Currently, setting \"Thread Model\" set to \"Separate\" won't work on Android: it'll just render a black screen and give numerous errors to the logs\r\n\r\nThis PR gets it working via two primary changes:\r\n\r\n1. Setting `egl_current_window_id` to `INVALID_WINDOW_ID` on `release_rendering_thread()`, so that we'll do `eglMakeCurrent()` on the main window when Godot's rendering thread calls `gl_window_make_current()`. (Without this change it won't do anything, because it thinks the main window is already current.)\r\n2. Making the Java render thread ignore errors from `eglMakeCurrent()` when creating a surface, if Godot is using a separate render thread. This is necessary in the case where the EGL surface is being re-created, because `eglMakeCurrent()` will fail on the Java render thread because Godot's render thread has already taken ownership of the EGL context -- but this is fine, since Godot's render thread will call `eglMakeCurrent()` later and succeed, and that's where all the rendering will happen anyway\r\n\r\nAdditionally, since we're using `eglGetCurrent*()` to get the various EGL resources, we will stash them on local variables whenever we can, since they'll only be available on the thread that called `eglMakeCurrent()`.\r\n\r\nThis PR builds on top of PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105529, and so it'll be marked as DRAFT until that one is merged\r\n\r\n## Original description (before 2025-08-04)\r\n\r\nCurrently, setting \"Thread Model\" set to \"Separate\" won't work on Android: it'll just render a black screen and give numerous errors to the logs\r\n\r\nThis PR gets it working via two primary changes:\r\n\r\n1. Allow Godot's rendering thread to take ownership of the EGL display, surface and context via `DisplayServerAndroid::gl_window_make_current()` (and later relinquish it via `DisplayServerAndroid::release_rendering_thread()`)\r\n4. Prevent the Java code from calling `eglSwapBuffers()` because its render thread no longer owns the EGL resources, and allow Godot's render thread to handle that on the C++ side (via `DisplayServerAndroid::swap_buffers()`)\r\n\r\nThe implementation is kind of messy because of the way the Java-side code is structured. If we refactored that so that less was done on the Java-side, and more responsibility was given to the C++ side (as well as switching to `android.opengl` so we can pass native handles back and forth), then it could be done more cleanly.\r\n\r\nHowever, I've taken the approach of making the smallest amount of changes to get this feature working. Given that the diff isn't that big, I think this could be fine for now?\r\n\r\n~~This depends on PR https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109057 and will be marked as DRAFT until it is merged~~","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097562,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc1NjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:android","name":"platform:android","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-m